EV

Purpose

EV (Extreme Voltage) is the fourth major electrical technology tier.

The player transitions from advanced industrial production to extreme-scale electrical infrastructure.

EV introduces significantly higher power requirements, advanced materials, complex chemical processing, high-throughput machinery, and production chains that require multiple interconnected industrial systems.

At this stage, the factory should begin operating as a large industrial complex rather than a collection of individual production lines.

Resources

EV primarily uses:

Steel
Aluminium
Titanium
Tungsten
Chrome
Nickel
Cobalt
Platinum
Gold
Copper
Advanced alloys
Rare industrial materials
Other materials required for extreme-voltage infrastructure

Higher-tier materials remain restricted until their respective technological stages.

Tools

EV introduces advanced industrial tools and equipment.

These tools should provide substantial improvements to construction, resource gathering, and industrial maintenance.

EV equipment should support large-scale industrial development without providing capabilities intended for IV and later tiers.

Processing

EV introduces highly complex multi-stage processing.

Production chains should increasingly require:

Advanced ore processing
Chemical processing
Advanced alloy production
Material purification
Specialized industrial components
High-tier machine components
Multi-stage chemical chains

Processing should require multiple specialized machines working together.

The player should increasingly rely on dedicated production facilities rather than general-purpose machines.

Machines

EV introduces high-performance industrial machinery.

Machines should provide:

Extreme-throughput material processing
Advanced chemical processing
Advanced alloy production
High-tier component manufacturing
Specialized material refinement
Large-scale industrial processing
Advanced automation

EV machinery should have significantly higher power requirements than HV machinery.

Power

Extreme Voltage becomes the primary power infrastructure.

The player must establish:

High-capacity power generation
Extreme-voltage distribution
Large-scale power storage
Reliable industrial power networks
Power infrastructure capable of supporting multiple EV machines simultaneously

Power generation and distribution should become a major engineering challenge.

Large production facilities should require dedicated power infrastructure.

Automation

EV introduces highly automated industrial production.

The player should be able to operate:

Large parallel production lines
Fully automated multi-stage processing
Advanced chemical factories
Automated alloy production
High-throughput material refinement
Large logistics networks
Automated component manufacturing

Automation should now be essential for progression.

The quantities of materials required by EV should make manual production impractical.

Create Integration

Create continues to provide mechanical and logistical infrastructure.

Create should primarily support:

Factory logistics
Large-scale material transportation
Mechanical automation
Material handling
Specialized mechanical processing
Industrial infrastructure

Create must not bypass EV technological requirements.

GregTech Integration

GregTech remains the primary technological progression system.

EV introduces advanced GregTech materials, machines, components, and processing chains.

GregTech progression should require complex industrial infrastructure and specialized production facilities.

EV production should prepare the player for the transition toward IV.

Modern Industrialization Integration

Modern Industrialization provides additional EV machinery and advanced processing capabilities.

Its systems should be integrated into the same technological progression and used for specialized production chains.

Modern Industrialization must not create an independent progression route that bypasses EV requirements.

Mekanism Integration

Mekanism provides advanced processing and industrial utility during EV.

Its machines may be integrated into specialized production chains but must remain subject to the same technological progression.

Mekanism must not provide unrestricted access to higher-tier processing or power systems.

Requirements

The player must complete HV before entering EV.

The player should have:

Established reliable HV electrical infrastructure
Automated essential HV production chains
Produced the components required for EV machinery
Established access to EV-tier materials
Built sufficient power generation and distribution infrastructure
Established advanced chemical and material processing
Automated the production of essential industrial components

Exit Condition

EV ends when the player has established an industrial complex capable of supporting the significantly greater complexity and power requirements of IV.

The player must:

Establish reliable EV power infrastructure
Automate essential EV production chains
Complete advanced chemical and material processing
Produce the components required for IV machinery
Establish the infrastructure necessary for IV production
Complete the required EV production chains

Completion of these requirements unlocks IV.

The EV stage should leave the player with a highly automated industrial complex capable of supporting multiple advanced production chains simultaneously.
